<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-acceptance-boundary> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Ignore claimed acceptedOutcome for authenticated acceptance accounting: acceptedOutcome and all authenticated accepted totals are null with status unverified. Count claimed accepted observations separately and expose no accepted-progress ratio. Failure/interruption/rejection are reported lifecycle classes, not independently authenticated outcomes. No generic truth flag, schema validity, exact digest or successful exit establishes semantic acceptance." <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-acceptance-boundary> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-clock-pairing> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "job-lifecycle-reader-clock-pairing" <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-clock-pairing> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementSeverity> <urn:usf:requirement-severity:blocking> <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-clock-pairing> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:validation> <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-clock-pairing> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "A start and one finish/failure/interrupted terminal pair must bind one clockDomainIdentity and identical start offset. Require safe nonnegative integers, end >= start and end-start=duration; total interval if present equals duration, and each reported subinterval is at most total duration. UTC is a separate real instant observation and may move backwards; never derive duration or monotonic order from UTC. Pending starts remain explicitly incomplete. Missing terminal offsets remain unknown and produce no duration sample. Unknown values require a nonempty bounded missingness reason." <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-clock-pairing> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-event-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "job-lifecycle-reader-event-identity" <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-event-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementSeverity> <urn:usf:requirement-severity:blocking> <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-event-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:validation> <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-event-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Recompute eventKey using canonicalDigest of the closed object {jobIdentity,workIdentity,attemptIdentity,phaseIdentity,eventKind}. Exact canonical-content replay deduplicates; a changed same-key event, multiple terminal kinds, changed pair source/scope/tool/route/work/owner/logical identity or clock domain refuses that attempt. Order is immaterial. Null attempt/work/logical/source identities are incomplete and unpairable, never one shared-null attempt. Refuse conflicting current logical-attempt reuse; never select the last received row as truth." <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-event-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-grouping> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "job-lifecycle-reader-grouping" <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-grouping> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementSeverity> <urn:usf:requirement-severity:blocking> <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-grouping> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:validation> <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-grouping> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Group comparable paired attempts by job type, phase, source, scope, tool and route, including explicit missingness. Report record/attempt/sample counts, refused and incomplete counts before min/max/median reported duration samples; no global duration sum, unqualified efficiency claim or distribution with no samples. Source/scope changes cannot join or share a replay identity. Stable deterministic lexical group ordering precedes max-items truncation. Do not echo event payloads, arbitrary missingness text, raw command arguments or private paths. Zero duration samples require null min/max/median; positive samples require finite numeric min <= median <= max within safe bounds. Compute median without unsafe integer addition. Source status observed requires the raw-byte digest; missing source requires null digest and zero input counts; stdin has null path and repository input has a validated metrics path. Actual readers must enforce these relationships in addition to schema shape." <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-grouping> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-overlap> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "job-lifecycle-reader-overlap" <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-overlap> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementSeverity> <urn:usf:requirement-severity:blocking> <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-overlap> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:validation> <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-overlap> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Detect parent cycles/missing parents and time overlap in the same clock domain. Parent-child intervals require their declared nonadditive disposition and matching actual parent identity; conflicting claimed none/accounted cannot waive observed overlap. Preserve individual duration samples but never sum nested or cross-job intervals. Report overlap pairs and incomplete parent linkage; offsets from different clock domains are incomparable, not disjoint. All interval kinds remain separate. Use half-open intervals [start,end); zero-duration intervals overlap none. Per clock domain use a sorted sweep and bounded active-end index/count with O(n log n) time and O(n) memory; never enumerate or materialize an all-pairs list. overlapPairs is the exact count, at most 4999950000 for the conservative 100000-record input bound. Include a confined many-overlaps fixture and a zero-duration/endpoint-touch case." <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-overlap> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-reader-reported-provenance> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "job-lifecycle-reader-reported-provenance" <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-reader> .
